2. The Linux kernel V3D and power-management drivers (GPL-2.0-or-later, Copyright (C) Broadcom)
   drivers/gpu/drm/v3d/ and drivers/pmdomain/bcm/bcm2835-power.c

   This driver's behaviour was checked against them throughout: the V3D interrupt enable and acknowledge order, the
   cache flush sequence including the GFXH-1897 erratum guard, the job submission order, and the power-down order of
   the ASB bus gates. Register names follow v3d_regs.h there.

3. RISC OS and ROOL's published sources and documentation (the kernel's GraphicsV handling, BCMSupport, BCMVideo, the
   OS_Memory and OS_DynamicArea documentation) were read to find out how the interfaces behave; they are not
   redistributed here.
